      "value": "@{5a766b8a0868b44b53569ce4|full_name}: Yeah I see your video. I don't know what's going on there.\nBut my point is if it's a separate camera, *none* of those settings matter. the separate camera doesn't need to write to depth, since it's all UI. it just renders UI with its own (mostly unused near&far clip plane) at its own position relative to playspace origin (near 0,0,0) no matter what you're doing in the world. it doesn't care if you've changed your world camera's near plane, or if you've done horizon adjust.\nEven if VRChat doesn't use a separate camera, they could emulate the same thing by overriding the view matrix in shader. literally pretend that the virtual menu/laser/UI camera is relative to the playspace no matter if you're 100000 units away from origin in game.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
